{"crc":"97e7887d","kind":"Candidate","payload":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that Django 3.2 raises W042 warnings for models that inherit a primary key from a parent model. The warning is about auto-created primary keys, but these models already have a primary key through inheritance.\n\nThe fix should be in the `_prepare` method of `Options` class in `django/db/models/options.py`. When a model has parents and the first parent link is promoted to be the primary key, we need to ensure the `auto_field` is set to avoid the W042 warning.\n\nLet me check the current code and provide the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/models/options.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        if self.pk is None:\n            if self.parents:\n                # Promote the first parent link in lieu of adding yet another\n                # field.\n                field = next(iter(self.parents.values()))\n                # Look for a local field with the same name as the\n                # first parent link. If a local field has already been\n                # created, use it instead of promoting the parent\n                already_created = [fld for fld in self.local_fields if fld.name == field.name]\n                if already_created:\n                    field = already_created[0]\n                field.primary_key = True\n                self.setup_pk(field)\n            else:\n                pk_class = self._get_default_pk_class()\n                auto = pk_class(verbose_name='ID', primary_key=True, auto_created=True)\n                model.add_to_class('id', auto)\n=======\n        if self.pk is None:\n            if self.parents:\n                # Promote the first parent link in lieu of adding yet another\n                # field.\n                field = next(iter(self.parents.values()))\n                # Look for a local field with the same name as the\n                # first parent link. If a local field has already been\n                # created, use it instead of promoting the parent\n                already_created = [fld for fld in self.local_fields if fld.name == field.name]\n                if already_created:\n                    field = already_created[0]\n                field.primary_key = True\n                self.setup_pk(field)\n                self.auto_field = field\n            else:\n                pk_class = self._get_default_pk_class()\n                auto = pk_class(verbose_name='ID', primary_key=True, auto_created=True)\n                model.add_to_class('id', auto)\n>>>>>>> REPLACE","round":1,"slot":0},"producer":{"instance":"01KZT2RPAQX6RYM33V26M24VV4","kind":"drafter","parent":"01KZT2RPAMZBMD5EHMJDSN1P88"},"schema":"Candidate@1","seq":14,"t":1786507984.262555}
{"crc":"05eb6057","kind":"substrate.TriggerFired","payload":{"factory":"validator","firing_key":null,"input_sha256":"sha256:a60fbf44e15c97d9b314adf398ffb2d40adc0a8e66700c1e87ac94481e5e3a79","instance":"01KZT2RZC6GTDA1A70Z0ZPJ54T","resolved_input":{"response":"Looking at the issue, the problem is that Django 3.2 raises W042 warnings for models that inherit a primary key from a parent model. The warning is about auto-created primary keys, but these models already have a primary key through inheritance.\n\nThe fix should be in the `_prepare` method of `Options` class in `django/db/models/options.py`. When a model has parents and the first parent link is promoted to be the primary key, we need to ensure the `auto_field` is set to avoid the W042 warning.\n\nLet me check the current code and provide the fix:\n\n# path: django/db/models/options.py\n<<<<<<< SEARCH\n        if self.pk is None:\n            if self.parents:\n                # Promote the first parent link in lieu of adding yet another\n                # field.\n                field = next(iter(self.parents.values()))\n                # Look for a local field with the same name as the\n                # first parent link. If a local field has already been\n                # created, use it instead of promoting the parent\n                already_created = [fld for fld in self.local_fields if fld.name == field.name]\n                if already_created:\n                    field = already_created[0]\n                field.primary_key = True\n                self.setup_pk(field)\n            else:\n                pk_class = self._get_default_pk_class()\n                auto = pk_class(verbose_name='ID', primary_key=True, auto_created=True)\n                model.add_to_class('id', auto)\n=======\n        if self.pk is None:\n            if self.parents:\n                # Promote the first parent link in lieu of adding yet another\n                # field.\n                field = next(iter(self.parents.values